he US have paved the way, I mean first and foremost the unacceptable, colonial-style agreement between the EU and the US to purchase $3.5 trillion worth of energy from the Americans over a three-year period, supposedly as a result of US concessions regarding trade tariffs imposed on the EU,\" the expert explained.\nOn January 26, the EU Council finalized a complete ban on Russian LNG supplies to the EU starting January 1, 2027, and on pipeline gas starting September 30, 2027. Meanwhile, the ban on LNG imports under short-term contracts took effect on April 25, 2026, and short-term pipeline gas supply contracts were set to expire by June 17, 2026.",
