        "title": "How fast is the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold charging speed?",
        "link": "https://www.androidcentral.com/phones/google-pixel/how-fast-is-the-google-pixel-11-pro-fold-charging-speed",
        "source": "Latest from Android Central",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:07:01.365080+00:00",
        "image": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Zi26XwYTrVCCDBwKUo3ELd-2048-80.jpg",
        "full_content": "How fast is the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold charging speed?\nThere's faster wireless charging, but not much else.\nHow fast is the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold charging speed?\nBest answer: The Pixel 11 Pro Fold can fast charge up to 50% in 30 minutes with a 30W or higher PPS charger. It now supports Qi2 (25W) wireless charging, which is 20% faster than the Pixel 10 Pro Fold.\nCharging speed of the Pixel 11 Pro Fold has improved, but at a big cost\nGoogle is boasting about how the Pixel 11 Pro Fold is the thinnest and lightest foldable it has produced, yet, but these gains have come at the cost of battery capacity. The Pixel 11 Pro Fold has a 4,750mAh battery, which is 265mAh less than the 10 Pro Fold. While the weight has dropped drastically to 239 grams (from 258 grams), it's still not as light as the Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra at 215 grams.\nBattery life claims for the Pixel 11 Pro Fold seem to be the same as the 10 Pro Fold, where Google is promising \"24+ hours\" on one charge. Fast wired charging is the same as well as the previous model. The only real improvement that I can see if the addition of Qi2 (25W) wireless charging.\nGoogle seems to be banking on the efficiency of the Tensor G6 SoC to make up for the loss in battery capacity, and I really hope it works out for its own sake. Google is on the back foot here when it comes to battery technology as Samsung and Motorola have both embraced silicon carbon battery tech for its respective 2026 foldables. The Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra packs a 5,000mAh battery capacity, while the Razr Fold has a 6,000mAh battery.\nI think Google took a big gamble here, putting a smaller battery in the Pixel 11 Pro Fold. Given its long-standing struggle trying to get Tensor to play nice with apps and its history with temperamental updates, this could go either way. I'm not sure if the Pixel 11 Pro Fold will make it to the list of the best Google Pixel phones, but maybe it will do better next year.\nThe lightest yet\nThe Pixel 11 Pro Fold finally gets comfortably slim and light, along with Qi2 (25) charging and the new HiLight feature. This is Google's best foldable to date and it has the price to match.\nGet the latest news from Android Central, your trusted companion in the world of Android\nRoydon has been writing about personal technology for 10+ years, and has covered everything from news, reviews, features, to on-ground coverage of big trade shows like CES. He's passionate about mobile technology and computing, dabbles with photography, and is still struggling to work his way through his Steam and PS4 game library.\nYou must confirm your public display name before commenting\nPlease logout and then login again, you will then be prompted to enter your display name.",
        "content": "How fast is the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold charging speed?\nThere's faster wireless charging, but not much else.\nHow fast is the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold charging speed?\nBest answer: The Pixel 11 Pro Fold can fast charge up to 50% in 30 minutes with a 30W or higher PPS charger. It now supports Qi2 (25W) wireless charging, which is 20% faster than the Pixel 10 Pro Fold.\nCharging speed of the Pixel 11 ...",
