at should have been given to him in good time before the trial starts. This is purely to be fair. We seek an adjournment,” defence said. To put an end to the back and forth over late issuance of statements, defence pleaded that they be furnished with all original statements today.\nState prosecutor Modibedi Tladi acceded to the submission made by defence. “We subscribe to the notion and we don’t oppose the adjournment,” Tladi said. After listening to the two sides, Regional Magistrate Mareledi Dipate agreed that the defence should not be ambushed. “The State should give the statements before the end of today so that we don’t ambush them. The trial will continue tomorrow,” Dipate ordered.",
