gy of the DCI-P3 colour gamut.\nFor picture processing, the television is powered by TCL’s AiPQ Engine, which includes technologies designed to improve contrast, colour, clarity and motion. Not only that but it also supports Dolby Vision and HDR10+ for compatible content.\nOn the smart TV front, the TCL’s T6D runs on Google TV and comes with 16GB of storage and 2GB of RAM. Moreover, it also boasts built-in Google Assistant for voice-based controls. The TV supports Dolby Atmos and features built-in stereo speakers. The 43-inch model can give you an audio output of up to 24W.\nYou also get three HDMI ports, including support for HDMI eARC, along with one USB port. For wireless connectivity, the TV supports dual-band Wi-Fi on both 2.4GHz and 5GHz networks, as well as Bluetooth 5.2 or 5.4 depending on the screen size.\nBhaskar is a Senior Copy Editor at Digit India who keeps a close watch on everything shaping the world of technology from smartphones and home appliances to AI, government tech initiatives, digital safety, and the latest industry developments. Whether it's breaking news, in-depth features, hands-on reviews, practical how-to guides, or exclusive scoops, he translates complex tech into stories that are easy to understand and worth reading. His work has been featured in iGeeksBlog, GuidingTech, and other leading publications. Before joining Digit India, he served as an assistant editor at TechBloat. A B.Tech graduate and full-time tech journalist, he is driven by just one goal, which is to help readers stay informed, stay secure, and stay ahead in an ever-changing digital world. View Full Profile",
