        "full_content": "Srinagar: After evading police for 35 years, a terrorist responsible for the 1991 Jammu railway station bomb blast was arrested in Anantnag district, police said on Thursday.\nPolice said accused Altaf Hussain Sheikh was brought before the TADA Court, and further legal proceedings will be initiated.\nThey said Sheikh had concealed his identity and been living as a businessman.\nAccording to the police, aSheikh, along with three other accomplices, carried out the bombing at platform number 1, killing three people, including two paramilitary personnel, and injuring 18 civilians.\nWhile one operative, Aman Ullah Khan, was arrested on the day of the blast, the other three went into hiding.\nOn Thursday, the Jammu Railway Police traced Sheikh to Anantnag and arrested him.\nAlso read: SIA searches nine locations across J&K in 1990 double murder case of Kashmiri Pandit writer and his son\n\"Railway (GRP) Police Jammu arrests an absconding terrorist booked under the Terrorist and Disruptive Activities (Prevention) Act. Altaf Hussain Sheikh, son of Nazir Ahmed Sheikh, resident of Marhama-Bijbehara, Anantnag, after a long chase of 35 years, initially went underground and was living with a concealed identity for several decades,\" police said in a statement.\n\"During the investigation, one accused, Aman Ullah Khan, was arrested, while three other accused persons escaped and could not be arrested at that time and were declared absconders by the concerned court,\" the police said.\nPolice said that the Railway police intensified their manhunt over the past two years, eventually finding him disguised as a successful businessman in the Bijbehara area.\n\" In the last two years, the railway police, Jammu, launched an intensive manhunt and identified the accused Altaf Hussain Sheikh, verified his identity by minutely going into details of his identity and residential particulars and discovered him living under a concealed identity, establishing himself as a