        "full_content": "Alberni unifies entity formation, global employment law, and compliance operations across 150+ international locations\nBorderless AI, the AI-native global employment platform, today announced the launch of Alberni, the AI-powered legal operating system for global employment law and global entity management. Alberni combines legal expertise with custom AI agents, allowing companies to hire and operate internationally without building a legal department in every country.\nManaging a global team requires not only best-in-class payroll but also best-in-class employment law and compliance. Every new market brings different localized legal and workplace compliance requirements. Until now, companies have managed it all with a patchwork of local law firms, consultants, and spreadsheets, at a cost that scales with every hire and every border crossed.\nAlberni was designed to eliminate the need for patchwork solutions. Borderless AI created Alberni as a single platform that pairs legal expertise with in-house AI, enabling companies to maintain a compliant global workforce footprint. This allows companies to handle everything from local entity formation and maintenance to worker classification, statutory deadlines, regulatory change, and workforce disputes. Deep legal expertise sets the foundation; AI makes it fast, consistent, and always on. This means companies no longer have to choose between moving quickly and staying compliant.\nThe launch comes as AI is rapidly transforming how law firms and in-house legal teams operate. Reports show a clear increase in the use of generative AI by firms and legal departments, with nearly half reporting use of AI in 2026 compared to just one quarter last year. There is a growing wave of new generation AI-native law firms, built without billable hours and staffed by lawyers working alongside AI.\nHowever, legal AI is largely focused on law firms and litigators. Alberni brings the same legal expertise directly to companies. The companies for whom global compliance is a daily operational reality, not a matter for outside counsel. Global employment requires more than legal knowledge. It requires infrastructure, operational experience, and systems that scale. By combining Borderless AI’s global operations know-how with legal expertise, Alberni makes a company’s global operations compliant by default in every jurisdiction in which it operates.\n“Companies have always faced a barrier to hiring globally while remaining compliant; every new market means more law firms, more retainers, and more risk,” says Willson Cross, CEO and Co-founder of Borderless AI. “We built Alberni so legal and regulatory compliance works like infrastructure: always on, always current, and smarter with every case. The companies that define the next decade will hire everywhere. We’re giving teams an easier and safer way to make that happen.”\nWith Alberni, companies get:\n- Entity infrastructure — legal entity formation, maintenance, and compliance monitoring across 150+ jurisdictions, with speed to market in every new region.\n- Compliance operations — worker classification workflows, statutory deadline tracking, regulatory monitoring, and workforce dispute management.\n- AI-powered legal intelligence — AI case intake, case analysis grounded in historical outcomes, automated scheduling of deadlines and procedures, document generation, and a caseload intelligence dashboard.\n- Compounding context — every entity, case, and jurisdiction lives in one system, so advice gets more tailored the longer you work with Alberni, and accountability transfers to purpose-built infrastructure instead of a growing legal headcount.",
