        "title": "IN PHOTOS | Perseids dazzle in the night sky",
        "link": "https://www.cbc.ca/news/science/photos/perseid-meteor-shower-photo-scroller-9.7305813?cmp=rss",
        "source": "CBC | Top Stories News",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:06:17.926216+00:00",
        "image": "https://i.cbc.ca/ais/e582aa5c-1852-4416-a74a-9d9487bbc4d0,1786627883525/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C472%2C8256%2C4644%29%3BResize%3D620",
        "full_content": "IN PHOTOS | Perseids dazzle in the night sky\nMeteor shower, which began July 17, reaches its peak Thursday and Friday\nThe Perseid meteor shower occurs annually when Earth passes through the trail of debris left behind by Comet 109P/Swift-Tuttle.\nThe celestial event peaked overnight, coinciding with a new moon that provided ideal conditions for stargazers because moonlight did not interfere with the view. Check out the shooting stars below.\nHere, Perseid meteor streaks are seen across the sky at Mount Ramon in the Negev Desert, near the town of Mitzpe Ramon, Israel, early Thursday.\n(Jack Guez/AFP/Getty Images)\nPeople watch a meteor as it streaks across the sky at Visnjan Observatory, Croatia, on Wednesday evening.\n(Antonio Bronic/Reuters)\nA meteor streaks across the night sky above the Stone Dolls of Kuklica, near Kratovo, North Macedonia, early Thursday.\n(Robert Atanasovski/AFP/Getty Images)\nPeople gather around the Monument to the Unknown Hero to watch the Perseid meteor shower, on Mount Avala, near Belgrade, Serbia.\n(Andrej Isakovic/AFP/Getty Images)\nA meteor, top right, streaks across the night sky above the megalithic stone walls of the ancient Illyrian city of Daorson near Stolac, in southern Bosnia-Herzegovina.\n(Elvis Barukcic/AFP/Getty Images)\nA meteor with a green tail, centre, and the streaks of two satellites are seen from Jacobsdorf, Germany, during the Perseid meteor shower on Wednesday.\n(Patrick Pleul/dpa/The Associated Press)\nA Perseid meteor streaks across the night sky behind St. Mark's Tower, a 17th century coastal fortification near the village of Baħar iċ-Ċagħaq, Malta.\n(Darrin Zammit Lupi/Reuters)",
