        "full_content": "Nakhchivan attracts AZN 156.7 million in fixed capital investments\nNakhchivan, August 13, AZERTAC\nIn January-July 2026, investments in fixed capital in the Nakhchivan Autonomous Republic amounted to AZN 156.7 million, directed toward the development of the economy and social sectors. This represents a 30.9% increase compared with the same period last year, according to the Nakhchivan State Statistical Committee.\nDuring the reporting period, AZN 76.6 million, or 48.9% of total investments, was allocated to the production sector, while AZN 20.1 million, or 12.8%, was directed to the services sector, and AZN 60 million, or 38.3%, to the construction of residential buildings.\nOf the total investments in fixed capital, AZN 127.5 million, or 81.4%, was allocated directly to construction and installation works. This figure is 43% higher than in the corresponding period of the previous year.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\n- 13.08.2026 [20:15]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Kalbajar district\n- 13.08.2026 [17:22]\nNakhchivan’s foreign trade turnover rises by 31.1%\n- 13.08.2026 [15:59]\nGDP in Nakhchivan rises by 3.1 percent\n- 13.08.2026 [12:05]\nGoygol – Ordubad’s hidden gem, where four seasons unfold at once VIDEO\n- 12.08.2026 [19:48]\nTwo people injured as bulldozer hits landmine in Khojavend\n- 12.08.2026 [16:05]\nRegional DOST Center opens in Nakhchivan\n- 07.08.2026 [20:12]\n“Khojaly Encyclopedia” presented - shedding light on history\n- 05.08.2026 [14:42]\n27 more families relocated to Khojavend receive keys to new homes\n- 04.08.2026 [19:52]\nTurkish journalists visit Khankendi\nFire and explosion at munitions plant at Colleferro, South of Rome\n- 13.08.2026 [21:03]\nPassenger train derails in UK’s East Sussex\n- 13.08.2026 [20:47]\nEU electricity production sees record low coal share\n- 13.08.2026 [20:31]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Kalbajar district\n- 13.08.2026 [20:15]\nTop stories update\n- 13.0