        "full_content": "Peruvian publication highlights bilateral relations with Azerbaijan\nLima, August 13, AZERTAC\n“La Razón” newspaper of Peru has published an article highlighting the remarks by Foreign Minister Carlos Espá to mark the 205th anniversary of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\nAlongside the key priorities of Peru’s foreign policy, the article placed a particular emphasis on the development of relations between Peru and Azerbaijan.\nThe article described the reopening of Peru’s embassy in Baku as a significant decision, noting that Azerbaijan is not only strategically located in the South Caucasus but also stands as a crucial energy and trade hub.\nIt also highlighted Azerbaijan’s recent statements on investments in Peru, stressing that these developments offer considerable potential for enhancing cooperation between the two countries.\nThe publication also stressed that further advancing Peru’s diplomatic relations with Azerbaijan could open new avenues for cooperation in the political, economic, trade, and investment spheres. In this regard, the reopening of Peru’s embassy in Baku was reviewed as a significant step toward deepening bilateral ties.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\nFire and explosion at munitions plant at Colleferro, South of Rome\n- 13.08.2026 [21:03]\nPassenger train derails in UK’s East Sussex\n- 13.08.2026 [20:47]\nEU electricity production sees record low coal share\n- 13.08.2026 [20:31]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Kalbajar district\n- 13.08.2026 [20:15]\nTop stories update\n- 13.08.2026 [20:00]\nYoung members of Azerbaijani diaspora join 31st AFS Youth Assembly\n- 13.08.2026 [18:53]\nUK defends seizing shadow fleet tanker after Putin threat\n- 13.08.2026 [18:26]\nBaku to host world’s top beach wrestlers\n- 13.08.2026 [18:17]\nPeruvian publication highlights bilateral relations with Azerbaijan\n- 13.08.2026 [18:09]\nGeneral Manager highlights Türkiye’s petrochemical potential\n- 13.08.2026 [18:06]\nBurga