        "full_content": "Baku to host world’s top beach wrestlers\nBaku, August 13, AZERTAC\nThe world’s top young beach wrestlers will gather in Azerbaijan as the country hosts the U17 Beach Wrestling World Championships and the fourth stage of the Beach Wrestling World Series for the first time from August 27 to 29. Both prestigious events will be held at the Sea Breeze resort.\nOn August 27, nearly 150 young wrestlers representing 34 countries will compete for medals at the U17 Beach Wrestling World Championships. The boys’ competition will feature 60kg, 70kg, 80kg and 90kg weight categories, while the girls will compete in the 45kg, 55kg, 65kg and 75kg categories.\nThe competition will continue on August 28-29 with the fourth stage of the senior Beach Wrestling World Series. Up to 60 athletes are expected to compete, with men’s events held in the 70kg, 80kg, 90kg and +90kg weight categories, and women’s events in the 50kg, 60kg, 70kg and +70kg categories.\nIn total, more than 200 athletes from 34 countries will compete for medals on the shores of the Caspian Sea.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\n- 13.08.2026 [16:44]\nIstanbul to host 2027 Spanish Super Cup featuring Barca, Madrid\n- 13.08.2026 [15:23]\nDoku signs new contract extension\n- 13.08.2026 [11:28]\nPSG edge out Aston Villa 2-1 to win back-to-back UEFA Super Cups\n- 12.08.2026 [17:30]\nAzerbaijani wrestlers ready for action at U20 World Championships\n- 12.08.2026 [15:58]\nRoma sign Nahuel Molina\n- 12.08.2026 [09:55]\nFenerbahce advance to Champions League playoffs with 1-0 win over Sturm Graz\n- 11.08.2026 [17:28]\nNapoli agree €6m deal with Fenerbahce to sell Romelu Lukaku\n- 11.08.2026 [17:17]\nAzerbaijan names 16 fighters for World Championships in Kazakh wrestling\nFire and explosion at munitions plant at Colleferro, South of Rome\n- 13.08.2026 [21:03]\nPassenger train derails in UK’s East Sussex\n- 13.08.2026 [20:47]\nEU electricity production sees record low coal share\n- 13.08.2026 [20:31