        "full_content": "Landmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Kalbajar district\nBaku, August 13, AZERTAC\nA mine incident occurred in the village of Sariyel village of the liberated Kalbajar district, on August 13,” the General Prosecutor's Office, the Ministry of Internal Affairs, and the National Agency for Mine Action (ANAMA) said in a joint statement.\nAccording to the statement, Suleymanov Kamran Shukur oglu, a resident of the Gaynag village of Tartar district, born in 1953, sustained an injury in a landmine explosion, while grazing animals in the pasture area that has not yet been cleared of mines.\n“The incident is currently under investigation by the Kalbajar district prosecutor’s office,” the statement said.\nANAMA, the Ministry of Internal Affairs, and the General Prosecutor's Office have urged citizens to adhere to safety rules, heed mine warning signs, and avoid unfamiliar areas.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\n- 13.08.2026 [20:00]\nTop stories update\n- 13.08.2026 [17:26]\nNakhchivan attracts AZN 156.7 million in fixed capital investments\n- 13.08.2026 [17:22]\nNakhchivan’s foreign trade turnover rises by 31.1%\n- 13.08.2026 [16:43]\nAnother shipment from Russia dispatched to Armenia via Azerbaijan\n- 13.08.2026 [15:59]\nGDP in Nakhchivan rises by 3.1 percent\n- 13.08.2026 [15:52]\nAzerbaijan’s Basel III reforms to strengthen loss absorption buffers\n- 13.08.2026 [12:20]\nThe Juma Mosque in Guba: A masterpiece of ancient architecture VIDEO\nFire and explosion at munitions plant at Colleferro, South of Rome\n- 13.08.2026 [21:03]\nPassenger train derails in UK’s East Sussex\n- 13.08.2026 [20:47]\nEU electricity production sees record low coal share\n- 13.08.2026 [20:31]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Kalbajar district\n- 13.08.2026 [20:15]\nTop stories update\n- 13.08.2026 [20:00]\nYoung members of Azerbaijani diaspora join 31st AFS Youth Assembly\n- 13.08.2026 [18:53]\nUK defends seizing shadow fleet tanker after Putin threat\n