        "full_content": "Fire and explosion at munitions plant at Colleferro, South of Rome\nBaku, August 13, AZERTAC\nA fire and an explosion hit a large munitions plant at Colleferro south of Rome Thursday, according to ANSA.\nThe blaze and blast occurred at the former Simmel Difesa plant, currently owned by Knds Ammo Italy.\nThe company produces medium and large-caliber ammunition for land and naval defense, as well as solid fuels for aerospace launchers.\nThe accident reportedly occurred in the powder pressing department.\nSeveral firefighting teams are on site but have not yet been able to intervene.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\n- 13.08.2026 [20:47]\nPassenger train derails in UK’s East Sussex\n- 13.08.2026 [20:31]\nEU electricity production sees record low coal share\n- 13.08.2026 [18:26]\nUK defends seizing shadow fleet tanker after Putin threat\n- 13.08.2026 [17:48]\nBurgas to host Eurovision Song Contest in 2027\n- 13.08.2026 [16:52]\nPoorest areas should not house all asylum seekers, says Burnham\n- 13.08.2026 [15:58]\nSouth Korea's Incheon airport becomes world's busiest for global traffic\nFire and explosion at munitions plant at Colleferro, South of Rome\n- 13.08.2026 [21:03]\nPassenger train derails in UK’s East Sussex\n- 13.08.2026 [20:47]\nEU electricity production sees record low coal share\n- 13.08.2026 [20:31]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Kalbajar district\n- 13.08.2026 [20:15]\nTop stories update\n- 13.08.2026 [20:00]\nYoung members of Azerbaijani diaspora join 31st AFS Youth Assembly\n- 13.08.2026 [18:53]\nUK defends seizing shadow fleet tanker after Putin threat\n- 13.08.2026 [18:26]\nBaku to host world’s top beach wrestlers\n- 13.08.2026 [18:17]\nPeruvian publication highlights bilateral relations with Azerbaijan\n- 13.08.2026 [18:09]\nGeneral Manager highlights Türkiye’s petrochemical potential\n- 13.08.2026 [18:06]\nBurgas to host Eurovision Song Contest in 2027\n- 13.08.2026 [17:48]\nNakhchivan attracts AZN 156.7 mi