        "full_content": "Kinetic Publishing and Electric Saint have announced Crescent County, a cosy adventure that sees you make deliveries during the day and take part in races during the night, all on awesome sci-fi inspired 'motorbrooms'.\nBoasting some lovely, colourful visuals, Crescent County has been confirmed for PC and consoles and will launch in Summer 2027. The debut showcase features an interview with creative director Anna Hollinrake as she breaks down its conception and development.\n“Crescent County is centred around the idea of what it means to find your home. We want players to enjoy every element of this - from taking part in blood-pumping racing to getting involved in messy local gossip and dating their friends. The motorbroom driving isn’t about time trials or leaderboards - it’s about hanging out with your friends, and above all, it should be fun!\n“Crescent County has been a passion project since 2017, grounded in magical realism and my own lived experience. It’s so exciting to now be working with the team at Kinetic Publishing to help bring it to life, and we can’t wait for players to lose themselves in the wonderful world of Mor!”\nLet's check out the key features:\n- Motorbroom driving: Enjoy crunchy, flow-state driving - deliver parcels to earn an income or race your island friendsc\n- Relationship building: Form deep relationships with the close-knit characters you meet, and get to know their joys, struggles, and endless drama\n- Open world: The Isle of Mor offers a painterly witch-tech open world to get lost in\n- Customisation: Upgrade your motorbroom (for handling, deliveries, AND aesthetics)\nKinetic Publishing has also revealed Precognition, the new horror from creators Sam Barlow and Brandon Cronenberg, scheduled to launch on Switch 2 in Spring 2028.",
