        "title": "Guide: Pokémon Pokopia Fetching Scales For Feebas Event Guide, From Prism Scales To Milotic",
        "link": "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/pokemon-pokopia-fetching-scales-for-feebas-event-guide",
        "source": "Nintendo Life | Latest Updates",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:06:17.925101+00:00",
        "image": "https://images.nintendolife.com/c97d683268603/large.jpg",
        "full_content": "The Fetching Scales for Feebas event runs from 13th August to 28th August, 2026, adding two Gen 3 Water-types to Pokémon Pokopia.\nIf you've played previous limited-time events, you'll know what to expect. A new Pokémon, Feebas, will rock up outside a Pokémon Center, asking you to find a currency in exchange for new items, helping you construct several brand new habitats.\nThis Pokémon Pokopia guide explains how to start the Fetching Scales for Feebas event, how to get Prism Scales, and everything you need to find Feebas evolution Milotic.\nHow To Start The Fetching Scales for Feebas Event\nBefore you start, you need to have rebuilt a Pokémon Center, and play between the dates of 13th August to 28th August, 2026.\nAs with recent live-events Wish Upon A Jirachi and Hide-and-Sneak, you couldn't time travel to this event ahead of time. However, now the start date as passed, once you've connected the game to the internet to authenticate the date, you are able to time travel back if you have already missed it.\nWhen you log in during the above dates, Feebas will appear outside of the Withering Wastes Pokémon Center and ask for you Prism Scales. Once you have enough, you can then trade them for event-specific items, and build two unique habitats.\nHow To Get Prism Scales\nTo get Prism Scales, you must visit Dream Islands with the help of Drifloon by interacting with a doll.\nOnce in a Dream Island, look out for flat, pink and blue shell-like items on the ground.\nIn our experience, these are only found on beaches or sandy environments, and we found a lot more in the Basin Dream Island, which is found by visiting the Starmie Doll discovered in the Bubbly Basin DLC.\nAll Fetching Scales for Feebas Event Items\nWhen you have some Prism Scales, you can head to the Pokémon Center and exchange them at the counter for event-specific items. These are:\n| Item | Prism Scales Cost | Needed for Event Habitat? | \n|---|---|---|\n| Beach Volleyball Set | 15 | Yes | \n| Sand Bed | 10 | Yes | \n| Swim Ring | 5 | Yes | \n| Big Swim Ring | 10 | Yes | \n| Floating Lantern | 10 | No | \n| Cooler | 10 | Yes | \nHow To Get The Exciting Beach and Marine Leisure Activities Event Habitats\nThe Fetching Scales for Feebas event has two habitats to unlock:\n| Habitat | Required items | Pokémon attracted | \n|---|---|---|\n| Exciting Beach |  | Feebas | \n| Marine Leisure Activities |  | Milotic | \nThis means you need to acquire a total of 50 Prism Scales (20 for Exciting Beach, 30 for Marine Leisure Activities) to unlock both. You could in theory just get enough for Milotic's habitat, but having Exciting Beach means you can then give Feebas a thematically suitable home once the event ends.\nThis isn't the first Pokémon Pokopia event we've covered. And if meeting Feebas and Milotic has inspired you to keep playing, our Pokémon Pokopia walkthrough leads the way to many more guides that can help.",
        "content": "The Fetching Scales for Feebas event runs from 13th August to 28th August, 2026, adding two Gen 3 Water-types to Pokémon Pokopia.\nIf you've played previous limited-time events, you'll know what to expect. A new Pokémon, Feebas, will rock up outside a Pokémon Center, asking you to find a currency in exchange for new items, helping you construct several brand new habitats.\nThis Pokémon Pokopia guide...",
