        "full_content": "The Pokémon Company has announced that it will be ending service for the 3DS app Pokémon Bank on 27th February 2027.\nSo this means that the ability to transfer creatures from Pokémon Bank to Pokémon Home will cease from that date. The company has advised users to ensure that any Pokémon stored in Bank are transferred over to Home prior to the closure.\nPokémon Home, of course, will continue service, and it's also been announced that Pokémon FireRed and LeafGreen for the Switch eShop will be added in October. As expected, it's been advised that any Pokémon transferred from the games to other entries won't be able to come back, and you also can't bring Pokémon from other games over to FireRed and LeafGreen.\nIn addition, as a little bonus, it's been announced that if you manage to complete the Pokédex in FireRed and LeafGreen, you can claim Celebi in the mobile version of Pokémon Home.\nFans can also look forward to the launch of Pokémon Winds & Waves for the Switch 2 in 2027. Information is scarce at the moment, but we're definitely keen to see more in the coming months.",
