        "full_content": "HBO’s next DC Original series is Lanterns, which centers on Aaron Pierre’s John Stewart and Kyle Chandler’s Hal Jordan.\nThe show will be one of the final new entries of the summer, launching mid-August. From co-creators Chris Mundy, Damon Lindelof and Tom King, it watches recruit Stewart and Lantern legend Jordan get drawn into a dark, Earth-based mystery as they investigate a murder in the American heartland.\nFind the specifics of the Lanterns release rollout below:\nWhen does Lanterns premiere?\nThe show premieres in the popular Sunday night slot at 9 p.m. ET and PT on HBO and arrives on streamer HBO Max at the same time.\nWill new episodes of Lanterns arrive weekly or all at once? How many episodes are there?\nWatch on Deadline\nOne new episode will arrive per week on Sunday nights. There are eight episodes in the series total, meaning the finale will arrive Oct. 4.\nSee the full Lanterns release schedule below:\n- Sunday, August 16: Episode 1\n- Sunday, August 23: Episode 2\n- Sunday, August 30: Episode 3\n- Sunday, Sept. 6: Episode 4\n- Sunday, Sept 13: Episode 5\n- Sunday, Sept. 20: Episode 6\n- Sunday, Sept. 27: Episode 7\n- Sunday, Oct. 4: Episode 8 (FINALE)\nWho is in the cast of HBO and DC’s Lanterns?\nAlongside Pierre and Chandler, the cast also includes Kelly Macdonald, Garret Dillahunt, Poorna Jagannathan, Laura Linney, Jason Ritter, Ulrich Thomsen, Nathan Fillion, J. Alphonse Nicholson and Jasmine Cephas Jones.\nWho else is behind HBO and DC’s Lanterns?\nThe Lanterns pilot is co-written by Chris Mundy, Damon Lindelof, and Tom King. Mundy serves as showrunner. The first two episodes are directed by James Hawes, with Stephen Williams, Geeta Vasant Patel, and Alik Sakharov also tapped to direct. The series is executive produced by Mundy, Lindelof, King, James Gunn, Peter Safran, Ron Schmidt, and Hawes. Based on the DC comic characters from “Green Lantern.” The series hails from HBO in association with Warner Bros. Television and DC Studios.",
