        "title": "Christy Knowings Dies: Former Nickelodeon Star Of ‘All That’ Was 46",
        "link": "https://deadline.com/2026/08/christy-knowings-dead-1237033066/",
        "source": "Deadline",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:06:17.924888+00:00",
        "image": "https://deadline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/chriasty.jpg?w=1024",
        "full_content": "Christy Knowings, a cast member of Nickelodeon‘s ’90s hit All That, died Tuesday, August 11, after being removed from life support at a Los Angeles-area hospital, TMZ reports. She was 46.\nKnowing’s aunt, Tyleah Joseph, announced the death yesterday on Facebook, but a cause was not disclosed.\nAccording to TMZ, citing family sources, Knowing was placed on life support after suffering an asthma attack on Friday, August 7, that left her with brain damage. The family made the decision to take her off life support on Tuesday.\nAfter appearing on a failed 1997 Nickelodeon sketch comedy pilot called And Now This, Knowings joined the network’s All That the same year. She would spend three seasons on the popular show, which, at the time, included fellow cast members including Kel Mitchell, Kenan Thompson, Danny Tamberelli, Nick Cannon, Amanda Bynes and others.\nAmong her characters on All That were a dental assistant to Amanda Bynes’ dentist, Jessica from the recurring Whateverrr!!! skits, and newscaster Brenda Stone.\nWatch on Deadline\nRELATED: Ex-Nickelodeon Child Star Kianna Underwood Killed In NYC Hit-And-Run\nFollowing All That, Knowings appeared in several episodes of Sesame Street from 2008 to 2011 alongside her real-life twin brother Chris Knowings, who was a more frequent actor on the series and had appeared in Spike Lee’s 1994 film Crooklyn.\nKnowings is the second former All That cast member to die this year following the fatal hit-and-run of Kianna Underwood last January in Brooklyn.\nIn her Facebook post last night, Knowings aunt wrote, “My brother Charles’ daughter Chrissy (Christy Knowings) has passed…She was a outstanding actress, comedian, twin sister, an amazing daughter….Rest in power Chrissy.”\nComplete information on survivors was not immediately available.",
        "content": "Christy Knowings, a cast member of Nickelodeon‘s ’90s hit All That, died Tuesday, August 11, after being removed from life support at a Los Angeles-area hospital, TMZ reports. She was 46.\nKnowing’s aunt, Tyleah Joseph, announced the death yesterday on Facebook, but a cause was not disclosed.\nAccording to TMZ, citing family sources, Knowing was placed on life support after suffering an asthma attac...",
