        "title": "How to Set Up Paytm Postpaid in Just a Few Minutes",
        "link": "https://paytm.com/blog/loan/postpaid-loan/how-to-set-up-paytm-postpaid-in-just-a-few-minutes/",
        "source": "A Comprehensive Guide to Money Transfer, Recharges, Bill Payments and Other Digital Payments | Paytm Blog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:06:17.923833+00:00",
        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2026/08/Paytm-Postpaid-Blog-1.png",
        "full_content": "Need a little extra flexibility for your payments? Paytm Postpaid gives you access to Credit on Paytm UPI, so you can spend now and pay next month.\nSetting up Paytm Postpaid is a simple, guided process that involves checking your offer, completing KYC, setting up UPI AutoPay and creating your Paytm Postpaid UPI PIN.\nHere’s a step-by-step guide to getting started.\nWhat is Paytm Postpaid?\nPaytm Postpaid is a Buy Now, Pay Later facility that gives you a short-term credit limit that you can use for payments and repay later. You can use it for both online and offline payments.\nYou can get a credit limit of up to ₹60,000 which may be upgraded based on your credit history and other factors.\nHow to Set Up Paytm Postpaid\nStep 1: Open the Paytm app\nOpen the Paytm app on your phone.\nYou can find Paytm Postpaid by:\n- Scrolling to the Financial Services section on the Paytm app homepage, or\n- Searching for “Postpaid” using the search bar.\nTap on Paytm Postpaid to begin the setup process.\nStep 2: Enter your PAN details\nEnter your PAN details as prompted.\nYour details will be used to evaluate your offer. Based on your credit history and other factors, you’ll see the credit limit available to you.\nStep 3: Review your offer and proceed\nOnce your offer is displayed, read the applicable terms and conditions carefully.\nIf you’re happy with the offer, tap “Proceed with this offer.”\nThere is no signup fee for setting up Paytm Postpaid, and there is no charge simply for signing up and not using the facility.\nStep 4: Complete Aadhaar verification\nAfter you proceed with the offer, the next steps may take a few seconds to process.\nYou’ll then complete the verification process with Suryoday Small Finance Bank, the lending partner for Paytm Postpaid.\nAn OTP will be sent to the mobile number linked to your Aadhaar.\nEnter the OTP and tap “Verify.”\nNever share your OTP with anyone.\nNext, enter your Aadhaar number, agree to the applicable terms and conditions, and tap “Perform KYC.”\nStep 5: Complete your KYC and selfie verification\nYour Aadhaar information will now be validated.\nYou may see a short processing screen while your details are being checked, followed by the selfie verification step.\nWhen prompted, submit your selfie.\nFor a smoother verification:\n- Make sure your face is clearly visible.\n- Use a well-lit place.\n- Avoid anything covering your face.\n- Follow the instructions displayed on the screen.\nIf required, you can retake your selfie until you’re satisfied with the result.\nStep 6: Give consent for credit bureau verification\nYou’ll then be asked to provide consent to Suryoday Small Finance Bank to collect, store and verify your credit information from different credit bureaus.\nRead the consent carefully before proceeding.\nThe verification can take up to 60 seconds. Stay on the screen during this process and do not press back or close the app.\nOnce the process is complete, you’ll see confirmation that your credit line has been approved.\nStep 7: Link your credit line\nOnce your credit line is approved, tap “Link credit line.”\nYou will be asked to provide some additional details, such as your email address, annual income and more. Enter the requested information and continue.\nStep 8: Set up UPI AutoPay\nNext, you’ll need to set up UPI AutoPay for your Paytm Postpaid repayments.\nThis is a required part of the setup and allows your repayments to be collected automatically when your bill is due.\nDuring setup, ₹1 will be debited from your bank account to verify the mandate. This amount is refunded.\nYou may also see a ₹15,000 mandate limit on the screen. This is the maximum amount of the AutoPay mandate and does not mean that ₹15,000 will be deducted from your account. The amount collected when your bill is due will be your applicable bill amount.\nReview the details, agree and proceed.\nStep 9: Sign the agreement\nYour details will be sent to Suryoday Small Finance Bank to complete the agreement.\nEnter your Aadhaar details and tap “Send OTP.”\nEnter the OTP you receive and tap “Verify.”\nYour agreement will then be digitally signed.\nStep 10: Set up your Paytm Postpaid UPI PIN\nYour Paytm Postpaid credit line now needs its own UPI PIN.\nSet it up just like you would set up a PIN for another Paytm UPI account.\nYou’ll be asked to complete Aadhaar verification again as part of setting up the PIN.\nOnce your PIN is successfully created, your Paytm Postpaid account is ready to use.\nStart using Paytm Postpaid\nThat’s it! Your Paytm Postpaid setup is complete.\nOnce activated, Paytm Postpaid will appear as a payment option when you make eligible payments. It can be used for payments across millions of stores, online websites and apps that accept Paytm UPI, and eligible recharges and bill payments on the Paytm app.\nWith Paytm Postpaid, you can get up to ₹60,000 credit limit, enjoy up to a 45-day credit period, and pay your bill the following month.",
        "content": "Need a little extra flexibility for your payments? Paytm Postpaid gives you access to Credit on Paytm UPI, so you can spend now and pay next month.\nSetting up Paytm Postpaid is a simple, guided process that involves checking your offer, completing KYC, setting up UPI AutoPay and creating your Paytm Postpaid UPI PIN.\nHere’s a step-by-step guide to getting started.\nWhat is Paytm Postpaid?\nPaytm Post...",
