        "title": "Paytm Pocket Money: Paytm UPI for Teens, with the Control Parents Need",
        "link": "https://paytm.com/blog/payment-gateway/paytm-pocket-money-paytm-upi-for-teens-with-the-control-parents-need/",
        "source": "A Comprehensive Guide to Money Transfer, Recharges, Bill Payments and Other Digital Payments | Paytm Blog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:06:17.923830+00:00",
        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2026/08/pocket-money-blog-1.png",
        "full_content": "Teaching teenagers how to manage money is one of the most valuable life lessons parents can give. From paying for lunch with friends to buying books or travel tickets, teens are starting to make everyday spending decisions on their own. The challenge is finding a way to give them that independence while still keeping things safe and manageable.\nThat’s exactly where Paytm Pocket Money comes in.Paytm Pocket Money helps teens make secure Paytm UPI payments while giving parents the control they need. It offers a simple way for young users to experience mobile payments while parents stay involved every step of the way.\nWhat is Paytm Pocket Money?\nPaytm Pocket Money is a feature that lets parents set up Paytm UPI payments for their teenagers while staying in control of their spending. Parents can add pocket money, keep an eye on spending, and guide their child’s financial journey, all from the Paytm app.\nIt strikes the right balance between independence and responsibility, making it easier for families to build healthy money habits together.\nWhy Parents and Teens Love It\nAs children grow older, they naturally want more independence. Parents, on the other hand, want peace of mind. With Paytm Pocket Money, both get exactly what they need.\nParents can:\n- Add pocket money whenever required.\n- Track spending easily.\n- Stay in control of how the account is used.\n- Teach responsible spending through everyday experiences.\nFor teens, it’s a simple way to make Paytm UPI payments for daily needs without depending on parents for every purchase. It also helps them learn budgeting and smarter spending from an early age.\nHow to Set Up Paytm Pocket Money\nGetting started is quick and easy.\n- Open the Paytm app and go to the Pocket Money section.\n- Enter your teenager’s mobile number.\n- Complete the verification process.\n- Set up the account and add pocket money.\n- Your teenager can then start making secure Paytm UPI payments using their own Paytm account.\nThe setup takes just a few minutes, making it easy for parents to introduce their children to safe and supervised mobile payments.\nSafe and Secure Payments\nWhen it comes to young users, security matters.\nEvery Paytm UPI payment is authorised using a secure UPI PIN, ensuring that only the account holder can complete a payment. At the same time, parents continue to have visibility into account activity, helping them guide their teenager’s spending habits with confidence.\nThis combination of security and parental oversight makes Paytm Pocket Money a reliable solution for families.\nBuilding Better Money Habits\nFinancial responsibility starts with small everyday decisions.\nWhether it’s managing weekly pocket money or deciding how to spend within a budget, Paytm Pocket Money gives teenagers practical experience in handling money responsibly. Parents can also use these moments to talk about saving, planning expenses, and making thoughtful financial choices.\nThese everyday lessons can go a long way in building lifelong confidence with money.\nGive Your Teen a Smarter Start\nPaytm Pocket Money makes it easy for teenagers to experience the convenience of mobile payments while giving parents the confidence of staying in control.\nWith secure Paytm UPI payments, parental supervision, and a simple setup process, it’s a practical way to help teens become financially responsible, one payment at a time.",
        "content": "Teaching teenagers how to manage money is one of the most valuable life lessons parents can give. From paying for lunch with friends to buying books or travel tickets, teens are starting to make everyday spending decisions on their own. The challenge is finding a way to give them that independence while still keeping things safe and manageable.\nThat’s exactly where Paytm Pocket Money comes in.Payt...",
