        "title": "How to Buy Digital Gold & Silver on Paytm in Just a Few Taps",
        "link": "https://paytm.com/blog/digital-gold/how-to-buy-digital-gold-silver-on-paytm-in-just-a-few-taps/",
        "source": "A Comprehensive Guide to Money Transfer, Recharges, Bill Payments and Other Digital Payments | Paytm Blog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:06:17.923812+00:00",
        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2026/08/silver-14.png",
        "full_content": "Remember the last time you thought, “I should probably start saving in gold”? Maybe you postponed it because you thought you needed a big amount. Or because buying gold meant finding a jeweler, checking prices, figuring out storage, and making time for the whole process.\nToday, you can skip most of that. Gold and silver can now be bought digitally, in amounts that fit your budget, straight from your phone. Whether you’re looking to make a one-time purchase or simply want to start building a habit, getting started can take just a few taps.\nHere’s how you can buy digital gold and silver on Paytm and make precious metals a little easier to fit into your everyday financial routine.\nWhat Is Digital Gold and Silver?\nBefore getting started, it helps to understand what buying digital metals means.\nDigital gold allows you to buy 24K gold in small quantities through a digital platform. Instead of receiving the physical metal immediately, the equivalent quantity is purchased on your behalf and securely stored in insured vaults backed by MMTC – PAMP.\nThe same idea applies to digital silver. You can purchase silver digitally without having to handle physical bars or coins at the time of purchase. This makes precious metals more accessible, particularly for people who want to start small rather than wait until they have enough money for a larger physical purchase.\nWhy Buy Gold or Silver Digitally with Paytm Gold?\nOne of the biggest advantages of buying digitally is convenience. You can buy gold or silver from your phone without planning a visit to a jewelery store. There is also no need to decide on jewelery designs, worry about making charges, or immediately arrange for physical storage.\nMore importantly, digital buying allows you to make smaller purchases. Instead of thinking, “I’ll buy gold when I have a few thousand rupees,” you can build the habit gradually. On Paytm Gold, for example, you can start your gold journey with as little as ₹21. That small starting point can make saving feel less intimidating and more achievable.\nHow to Buy Digital Gold on Paytm\nBuying digital gold doesn’t have to involve complicated steps. Here’s a simple walkthrough.\nStep 1: Open the Paytm App\nOpen the Paytm app on your smartphone and look for the Gold section.\nOnce you’re there, you’ll be able to view the current gold price and explore your buying options.\nStep 2: Enter the Amount You Want to Buy\nEnter the amount you want to invest based on your budget. Whether you want to start with ₹21 as a daily SIP or make a larger purchase, you can choose an amount that works for you.\nThe quantity of gold you receive is calculated according to the applicable live market price.\nStep 3: Review the Details\nBefore completing your purchase, review the amount, applicable GST and other relevant charges displayed on the platform.\nWith digital gold, the price you pay includes the applicable costs associated with the purchase. Unlike jewellery, there are no making charges involved.\nStep 4: Complete the Payment\nChoose your preferred payment method available on Paytm and complete the transaction.\nOnce the purchase is successful, the corresponding quantity of gold is reflected digitally in your account.\nThat’s it. Your gold purchase is done without having to step into a jewellery store. The process is the same for the silver too.\nWhere Is Your Digital Gold Stored?\nOne common question people have about digital gold is: “If I can’t see the gold, where is it?”\nWith Paytm Gold, the gold purchased is backed by physical 24K gold and stored securely in vaults operated by MMTC-PAMP.\nThis means your digital holding represents actual gold rather than simply being a number on your screen. The gold is stored securely, while you can view and manage your holdings digitally.\nGold or Silver: Which One Should You Buy?\nThere isn’t a universal answer.\nGold and silver have different characteristics, and the choice depends on your financial goals, preferences and risk considerations. Gold has traditionally been associated with long-term wealth preservation, family security and important life milestones. Silver, on the other hand, has a lower price per unit and can appeal to people who want to explore precious metals with a smaller starting amount.\nSome people may prefer gold, while others may want exposure to both. The important thing is to understand what you’re buying and choose an amount that fits comfortably within your overall financial plan.\nYou Don’t Have to Buy Only Once\nPerhaps the biggest shift digital precious metals bring is the ability to turn buying into a habit. Instead of making one large purchase every few years, you can make smaller purchases regularly.\nFor those who prefer a structured approach, Paytm Gold also offers Gold SIPs, allowing you to invest daily, weekly or monthly. You can start a Gold SIP with as little as ₹21/daily. For example, setting aside a small amount regularly can help you build a gold holding alongside your other financial goals without having to make a large upfront purchase. It’s less about the size of one purchase and more about building consistency over time.\nKeep an Eye on Gold Prices\nPrices can change regularly based on several factors, including global economic conditions, interest rates, currency movements, inflation expectations and investor demand. If you’re actively buying gold, keeping track of price movements can help you stay informed.\nPaytm Gold also offers features such as Price Alerts, which can help you keep an eye on gold prices without constantly checking them yourself. The goal isn’t necessarily to predict every price movement. Instead, it’s about making informed decisions and understanding the market you’re participating in.\nWhat Happens When You Want to Sell?\nBuying digital gold doesn’t mean you have to hold it indefinitely. When you decide to sell, you can initiate the sale digitally. The selling price is based on the applicable market price at the time of the transaction, while standard applicable costs are adjusted as per the platform’s terms.\nUnlike buying, GST isn’t charged again on the sale transaction. The proceeds from the sale are then processed according to the applicable payment and settlement process.\nA Simpler Way to Start Your Precious Metal Journey\nGold and silver don’t have to be purchases reserved only for weddings, festivals or major milestones. With digital precious metals, you can start small, buy when it suits you and manage your holdings from your phone.\nWhether you’re putting ₹21 into gold to begin a new savings habit, making a one-time purchase for a future goal, or exploring digital silver, the process can be as simple as a few taps. And sometimes, that’s all it takes to turn a traditional form of saving into a modern financial habit.\nStart small. Stay consistent. Let your goals grow with you.",
        "content": "Remember the last time you thought, “I should probably start saving in gold”? Maybe you postponed it because you thought you needed a big amount. Or because buying gold meant finding a jeweler, checking prices, figuring out storage, and making time for the whole process.\nToday, you can skip most of that. Gold and silver can now be bought digitally, in amounts that fit your budget, straight from yo...",
