        "full_content": "EXCLUSIVE: HBO‘s Task is rounding out its cast for Season 2, adding Stephanie Sigman (Nemesis), Alaíde (Rebelde), Rocío Guzmán (Down the Rabbit Hole) and Regina Nava (Blood Pact) in recurring roles.\nBased on an original idea by Brad Ingelsby, Task is set in the working-class suburbs outside of Philadelphia. An FBI agent heads a Task Force to put an end to a string of drug-house robberies led by an unsuspecting family man.\nIn Season 2, Tom Brandis (Mark Ruffalo) takes the helm of a new task force, but the deeper the operation runs, the harder it is to tell who’s the target.\nCast also includes Mahershala Ali as Eddie Barnes, Julianne Nicholson as Lori Ross, Harry Melling as Brennan Boylan, Adam Nagaitis as Luke Clemmons, Aminah Nieves as Nataly Zamora, Edgar Ramírez as Miguel Contreras, Martha Plimpton as Kathleen McGinty, and Silvia Dionicio as Emily Brandis.\nWatch on Deadline\nSigman plays Carmen Belandria, a no-nonsense, fiercely loyal mother and wife of Miguel.\nAlaíde portrays Maria Delgado, a sharp and resourceful cartel escapee fighting to reunite with her sister.\nGuzmán is Yvonne Delgado, an innocent yet fearless immigrant farm worker determined to protect her family.\nNava plays Fernanda, a resilient and stubborn immigrant mushroom farm worker.\nIngelsby serves as creator, writer, showrunner and executive producer. Additional executive producers include Paul Lee and Mark Roybal for wiip, Jeremiah Zagar, Ruffalo, and Ron Schmidt. Nicole Jordan-Webber and Karen Wacker co-executive produce. Casting is by Bialy Thomas & Associates.\nKnown for her work on S.W.A.T., Narcos and The Bridge, Sigman can currently be seen recurring in the Netflix series Nemesis from creator Courtney A. Kemp and recently appeared in Apple’s The Morning Show. She’ll also be seen in the upcoming Searchlight Pictures film Behemoth! alongside Pedro Pascal, Olivia Wilde and Will Arnett. Sigman is repped by Paradigm Talent Agency, Alchemy Entertainment and Yorn, Levine, Barnes.\nAlaíde, Guzmán and Nava are repped by Vision Entertainment.",
