        "title": "Top Benefits of Paytm AU Credit Card for Online and Offline Spending",
        "link": "https://paytm.com/blog/credit-card/paytm-au-credit-card-benefits/",
        "source": "A Comprehensive Guide to Money Transfer, Recharges, Bill Payments and Other Digital Payments | Paytm Blog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:07:01.361918+00:00",
        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2026/07/6612_CC_Blog_post.png",
        "full_content": "The Paytm AU Credit Card is built around one idea: every rupee you spend should grow into Paytm Gold. Whether you are booking a flight, paying a utility bill, or making a quick UPI transfer, the card converts your everyday transactions into real gold value, with 1 reward point equal to ₹1, redeemable directly into Paytm Gold with no conversion loss.\nIt is also lifetime-free. No joining fee, no annual fee, no renewal charges, ever. The reward system is equally transparent: you always know exactly what your points are worth and how to use them.\nWhat Is the Paytm AU Credit Card?\nThe Paytm AU Credit Card is a co-branded credit card issued by AU Small Finance Bank in partnership with Paytm. It is designed to work closely with the Paytm app, especially for UPI payments, recharges, bill payments, and other everyday transactions.\nOnce the card is activated, you can:\n- View your transactions and statements\n- Track reward points earned\n- Check available offers\nAll of this is accessible directly within the Paytm app, without needing to log in to a separate banking platform.\nThe card functions like a regular credit card in terms of billing cycles, credit limits, and repayments, but its usage and tracking are simplified through Paytm. This makes it particularly useful for users who already rely on Paytm for managing their daily payments.\nTop Benefits of the Paytm AU Credit Card\nThe Paytm AU Credit Card is designed to reward everyday spending across UPI, Paytm, and general purchases. Here is a detailed look at the key benefits and how they translate into real value.\nLifetime-Free Card with No Hidden Charges\nThe card comes with no joining fee, no annual fee, and no renewal charges. You can continue using it long term without worrying about meeting spending conditions or paying maintenance costs.\n5% Rewards on Paytm Travel and Gold\nYou earn 5% reward points on spends in Paytm Travel and Paytm Gold categories. Since 1 reward point equals ₹1, this translates directly into a 5% value back on these transactions, making it one of the highest rewarding categories on the card.\nHigh Rewards on Paytm UPI Transactions\nYou earn rewards every time you pay via UPI, with higher returns on Paytm:\n- 2% reward points on Paytm UPI transactions up to ₹2,000\n- 1% reward points on Paytm UPI transactions above ₹2,000\n- 0.25% reward points on UPI payments made through other apps\nThis makes Paytm UPI the most rewarding way to use the card for daily payments.\nRewards on Everyday Paytm Payments\nRoutine payments also earn rewards:\n- 1% reward points on recharges and utility bill payments via Paytm\nThis ensures your regular monthly expenses continue to generate value.\n1% Rewards on All Other Spends\nYou earn 1% reward points on all online and offline purchases, including shopping, dining, and retail transactions. This makes the card useful beyond the Paytm ecosystem as well.\nComplimentary Lounge Access – for You and Your Family\nYou can avail complimentary airport lounge access by completing a round-trip flight booking of ₹5,000 or more through the Paytm app using the card. This benefit extends to your family as well, so everyone travelling together can enjoy a more comfortable airport experience.\nFuel Surcharge Waiver\n- 1% fuel surcharge waiver\n- Maximum benefit of ₹100 per month\nFuel transactions do not earn reward points, but the surcharge waiver still applies as a separate benefit.\nBuild Wealth with Every Spend – Convert Rewards into Paytm Gold\nEvery reward point you earn holds real monetary value: 1 reward point = ₹1 in Paytm Gold, with no conversion loss and no hidden deductions. This means the card is not just a payment instrument. It is a way to steadily accumulate gold through purchases you would make anyway.\nA ₹10,000 travel booking earns ₹500 in Paytm Gold. A ₹5,000 monthly UPI spend earns up to ₹100 in gold. Over a year, consistent card usage across categories can translate into a meaningful gold holding, built entirely from everyday transactions, at no extra cost.\nYou can also use reward points to pay utility bills on Paytm, giving you flexibility if you prefer immediate savings over gold accumulation.\nSimple and Transparent Reward Value\n1 reward point = ₹1. No tiers, no expiry conditions to navigate, no conversion math. You always know exactly what your rewards are worth.\nAll-in-One Tracking Within the Paytm App\nOnce the card is active, you can manage everything inside the Paytm app, tracking transactions, monitoring reward points, and viewing applicable offers, all in one place without switching platforms.\nUnderstanding the Reward Capping\nThe Paytm AU Credit Card applies monthly reward limits across different spending categories. These caps help structure how rewards are earned while still allowing consistent value on regular usage.\n- UPI spends: up to 1,000 reward points per month\n- Paytm and e-commerce spends: up to 1,000 reward points per month\n- Offline and POS spends: up to 1,000 reward points per month\nEach category has its own separate cap, so you can continue earning rewards across multiple types of spending within the same month.\nTransactions Not Eligible for Reward Points\nWhile the card rewards most everyday spending, certain categories are excluded from earning reward points as per standard credit card policies. Being aware of these exclusions helps you plan your usage better and maximise rewards where they apply.\nThe following transactions do not earn reward points:\n- Wallet reloads\n- Jewellery and gold purchases\n- International transactions\n- EMI transactions\n- Rent and real estate payments\n- Insurance payments\n- Education-related payments\n- Government services\n- Fuel transactions\n- Utility bill payments\nThese categories are typically excluded across most credit cards due to their nature or regulatory considerations. You can still use your card for these payments, but reward points will not be applicable on such transactions.\nNote on utility and recharge payments: Utility and recharge payments made via the Paytm app earn 1% rewards within the monthly cap. Utility transactions processed outside the Paytm app, or beyond the monthly cap, are not eligible for reward points.\nThe Four Core Value Propositions at a Glance\nHow Does the Paytm AU Credit Card Compare?\nA one-time welcome bonus is a useful head start, but the Paytm AU Credit Card’s ongoing 5% Travel and Gold rewards, family lounge access, and direct Paytm Gold accumulation deliver compounding value the longer you use the card. For users already in the Paytm ecosystem, the returns over 12 months of regular usage will outpace a single activation benefit offered by most competing cards.\nWho Should Apply for the Paytm AU Credit Card?\nThe Paytm AU Credit Card is best suited for users whose spending is closely aligned with UPI and the Paytm ecosystem. It works particularly well if your daily payments and bookings are already digital-first.\nThis card is a strong fit if you:\n- Use Paytm UPI regularly for everyday payments\n- Book flights, trains, or buses through the Paytm app\n- Want a lifetime-free credit card with no annual fee commitment\n- Prefer a simple reward system where 1 point equals ₹1\n- Use Paytm for recharges, bill payments, or digital gold purchases\n- Want basic travel benefits like lounge access without opting for a premium card\nHere is how the card maps to specific spending profiles:\nHigh-volume Paytm UPI users (₹10,000+ monthly UPI spend): If you spend ₹10,000 or more per month via Paytm UPI, you can earn up to ₹200 in Paytm Gold every month. ₹400 on the first ₹20,000 at 2%, and ₹100 on the remaining ₹10,000 at 1%, subject to the monthly category cap of 1,000 reward points.\nRecharge and utility bill payers: If you use Paytm regularly for mobile recharges, DTH, electricity, and other utility bills, you earn 1% on every eligible payment within the monthly cap, converting routine expenses into Paytm Gold.\nPaytm Travel bookers (₹3,000–₹15,000 in travel bookings): Every rupee spent on Paytm Travel earns 5% back in reward points. A ₹10,000 flight booking earns ₹500 in Paytm Gold, and the same booking qualifies you for complimentary airport lounge access for your entire family.\nPaytm Gold investors: If you use Paytm to purchase digital gold, every transaction earns 5% back, allowing you to compound your gold holdings over time through regular purchases.\nPaytm ecosystem loyalists (₹20,000–₹1,00,000 monthly spend across 2–4 cards): For users who centralise spending and bill payments through the Paytm app, every eligible category contributes reward points simultaneously. UPI, travel, and recharges, with separate caps ensuring you can earn across all three in a single month.\nIt may be less suitable if you:\n- Spend heavily on categories like insurance, education, or rent\n- Frequently make international transactions\n- Prefer reward programmes that offer broader redemption options outside the Paytm ecosystem\nHow to Apply for the Paytm AU Credit Card\nApplying takes only a few minutes, entirely within the Paytm app:\n- Open the Paytm app and go to the Loans & Credit Cards section\n- Select the Paytm AU Credit Card\n- Tap Apply Now\n- Enter your basic details and complete KYC verification (PAN and Aadhaar-based verification, if required)\n- Submit your application\nOnce submitted, you can check your eligibility status and track your application; both are available directly within the Paytm app.\nActivate early: Once your card is approved, activate it within 5 days to unlock rewards from your very first UPI spend.\nFinal Thoughts\nThe Paytm AU Credit Card is the most rewarding option for users already spending through the Paytm ecosystem. At 5% on Travel and Gold, up to 2% on UPI, family lounge access on Paytm flight bookings, and a lifetime-free structure, the card covers every major spending category without adding cost.\nWhat makes it different is the reward destination. Every point goes into Paytm Gold at a fixed ₹1=₹1 rate, with no conversion loss. That means the longer you use the card, the more gold you accumulate, across flight bookings, UPI payments, recharges, and everyday purchases. A welcome bonus from a competing card gives you value once. This card gives you a percentage of every transaction, indefinitely.\nIf your spending is already centred around Paytm, there is no reason to wait. Open the Paytm app, go to Credit Cards, and apply for the Paytm AU Credit Card today.\nIf you’re using a mobile device, tap the provided link. If you’re on a desktop, scan the QR code to continue.",
        "content": "The Paytm AU Credit Card is built around one idea: every rupee you spend should grow into Paytm Gold. Whether you are booking a flight, paying a utility bill, or making a quick UPI transfer, the card converts your everyday transactions into real gold value, with 1 reward point equal to ₹1, redeemable directly into Paytm Gold with no conversion loss.\nIt is also lifetime-free. No joining fee, no ann...",
