        "title": "Make Every Paytm UPI Payment More Secure with Biometric Authentication on Paytm",
        "link": "https://paytm.com/blog/payment-gateway/make-every-paytm-upi-payment-more-secure-with-biometric-authentication-on-paytm/",
        "source": "A Comprehensive Guide to Money Transfer, Recharges, Bill Payments and Other Digital Payments | Paytm Blog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:07:01.361915+00:00",
        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2026/08/Biometric-6.png",
        "full_content": "There are some everyday moments when you realise just how much your phone does for you. Ordering food, booking a cab, splitting a bill, or making a quick payment at your favourite café can all happen in a few taps.\nAnd now, Paytm UPI payments are getting even more convenient with biometric authentication on Paytm.\nWith Paytm, UPI payments can now be verified using your fingerprint on Android or Face ID on iPhone, so you don’t always have to enter your UPI PIN. It is a small change, but one that can make everyday mobile payments feel much faster and smoother.\nYour Face or Fingerprint Can Verify Your Payment\nWe’ve all been there. You’re in a hurry, there’s a queue behind you, and you’re trying to remember your UPI PIN before the payment goes through.\nWith biometric authentication on Paytm, that extra step can be skipped for eligible payments up to ₹5,000. You can simply use your fingerprint or Face ID to verify the payment. For payments above ₹5,000, your UPI PIN is required. And if you prefer using your UPI PIN for an eligible payment, that option is still available.\nThe idea isn’t to change how you make UPI payments completely. It is simply about giving you another convenient way to verify them.\nWhy biometric authentication on Paytm Feels More Convenient\nThe biggest advantage is pretty straightforward: less friction.\nYour fingerprint and Face ID are already part of how you unlock and use your phone. Bringing that familiar experience into Paytm UPI payments means you can authenticate eligible payments without manually entering your UPI PIN every time.\nIt can also be useful when you’re making a payment in a busy public place. Instead of entering your PIN where people around you might see your screen, biometric authentication gives you another way to verify an eligible payment.\nIt feels less like learning something new and more like your phone quietly getting better at something you already do every day.\nYour Phone Can Also Help You Access Cash\nThe convenience doesn’t stop at Paytm UPI payments.\nAt supported ATMs, Paytm users can make cardless ATM withdrawals using UPI. Simply select the UPI Cash Withdrawal option on the ATM, scan the QR code using Paytm, and authenticate the withdrawal using Face ID, fingerprint, or your UPI PIN.\nThat means your phone can handle another everyday task without needing a debit card.\nA Small Upgrade to Everyday Mobile Payments\nTechnology is most useful when it makes everyday things feel simpler without making them complicated.\nBiometric authentication on Paytm does exactly that for eligible Paytm UPI payments. You get the choice of using Face ID or fingerprint for eligible payments up to ₹5,000, while your UPI PIN remains available when required.\nAdd cardless ATM withdrawals at supported ATMs, and your phone is becoming much more useful for everyday financial tasks.\nSometimes, the best technology upgrade is the one you barely have to think about.",
        "content": "There are some everyday moments when you realise just how much your phone does for you. Ordering food, booking a cab, splitting a bill, or making a quick payment at your favourite café can all happen in a few taps.\nAnd now, Paytm UPI payments are getting even more convenient with biometric authentication on Paytm.\nWith Paytm, UPI payments can now be verified using your fingerprint on Android or Fa...",
