        "content": "The Go Blog\nAllocating on the Stack\nWe’re always looking for ways to make Go programs faster. In the last 2 releases, we have concentrated on mitigating a particular source of slowness, heap allocations. Each time a Go program allocates memory from the heap, there’s a fairly large chunk of code that needs to run to satisfy that allocation. In addition, heap allocations present additional load on t...",
