        "image": "https://ubuntu.com/wp-content/uploads/9336/Social-Media-announcement-new-certified-board.png",
        "full_content": "Advantech AOM-2721 is now Ubuntu Certified\nMikhail Khazov\non 13 August 2026\nTags: Advantech , Certified hardware , Edge AI , IoT , Ubuntu Pro for Devices\nCanonical announces that the Advantech AOM-2721 is officially joining the list of Ubuntu Certified Hardware. This latest certification highlights the deepening collaboration between Canonical and Advantech.\nWith full certification for Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, developers utilizing Advantech’s powerful Open Standard Module (OSM) AOM-2721 can now deploy a seamless, securely designed, and highly optimized Ubuntu experience right out of the box.\nTiny size, massive edge power\nThe Advantech AOM-2721 is a highly compact Size-L OSM. Measuring just 45 x 45 mm, this miniature solder-on module is designed to outpace traditional computer-on-modules. At its core lies the Qualcomm® Octa-core QCS6490 processor operating with a 6.9-watt TDP.\nThis architecture allows the AOM-2721 to deliver robust on-site computing. In fact, according to Advantech, the QCS6490 achieves nearly 20% better performance compared to mid-tier x86 processors, while providing an impressive 43-75% reduction in power consumption. This makes it an unparalleled solution tailored to meet the demanding physical and thermal constraints of diverse AIoT scenarios and handheld applications.\nEmpowering machine vision with on-device AI\nAs industries push intelligence closer to the edge, the AOM-2721 is perfectly equipped to handle intensive workloads. The module features 12 TOPS of AI capability, alongside support for dual-camera inputs and a native video codec.\nThis combination excels in applications requiring low-latency signals, seamless video capture, and resilience to vibrations within limited installation spaces. It is especially well-suited for autonomous mobile robots (AMR). By leveraging on-device AI, these AMRs can process data from cameras, radar, and LiDAR to perform complex tasks such as object detection, localization, route optimization, and collision avoidance. Furthermore, developers can utilize the Qualcomm AI Hub to streamline the deployment of machine learning models.\nAbundant interfaces and seamless connectivity\nTo fully integrate into modern AIoT ecosystems, the AOM-2721 offers a vast array of I/O options within its compact form factor. Key connectivity features include:\n- High-speed expansion: PCIe Gen3 support for 5G and Wi-Fi 6 connectivity.\n- Next-gen storage: High-speed memory and storage interfaces including LPDDR5 and UFS.\n- Versatile I/O: Flexible connectivity via USB 3.2, UART, and GPIO.\n- Rich displays: Dual-display capability supporting up to 2K resolution across DSI, DP, and eDP interfaces.\nWhen paired with Qualcomm’s 5G and Wi-Fi 6 modules, the integration of the Octa-core QCS6490 CPU ensures compatibility and minimal latency.\nUbuntu optimized for Qualcomm silicon\nJust as we expanded support with the Ubuntu general availability for Qualcomm Dragonwing, certifying the Advantech AOM-2721 ensures that developers can build, deploy, and scale their AIoT projects with confidence. Ubuntu certification means this device has passed rigorous testing to guarantee hardware components function flawlessly on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS at the time of certification and in the future. The Ubuntu Certification team performs regression testing on certified hardware on a regular cadence to ensure Ubuntu Stable Release Updates (SRU) are validated on certified hardware.\nCustomers deploying the AOM-2721 with Ubuntu will benefit from Canonical’s robust security patching, long-term support (LTS), and a vast ecosystem of open-source tools.\nMaximizing enterprise value with Ubuntu Pro for Devices\nFor commercial deployments requiring long-term reliability and compliance, companies can enhance their Ubuntu-powered fleet with an Ubuntu Pro for Devices subscription. This enterprise-grade service offers critical benefits for embedded and IoT deployments:\n- CVE Protection: Prompt security patches for critical and high-severity vulnerabilities for up to 15 years, minimizing exposure to security threats at the edge.\n- Device Management Solutions: Reduced cost of managing device fleets and proactive management of security for IoT devices.\n- Compliance and Hardening: Access to tools for automated security hardening and compliance profiles, such as CIS benchmarks and FIPS-compliant cryptographic modules.\nWhether you are building the next generation of autonomous robots or deploying smart industrial machine vision systems, the Advantech AOM-2721 powered by Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu Pro for Devices subscription provides the securely designed, optimized foundation you need to get to market faster.\nLearn more\nExplore our hardware ecosystems on the Ubuntu Certified Hardware Blog.\nFor more information about AOM-2721 contact your local Advantech sales representative or visit the Advantech official website.\nOpen source is what we do\nWe believe in the power of open source software. Besides driving projects like Ubuntu, we contribute staff, code and funding to many more.",
